  "term": "parkinsonism",
  "definition": "Parkinsonism is a group of disorders marked by impaired motor control, typically including slowness of movement, muscle stiffness, tremor, and problems with balance and posture. It includes primary, secondary, and inherited forms and is linked to dysfunction in dopamine-related movement pathways in the basal ganglia.",
